    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8348A\n\nSPONSOR: TEDISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to dedicating a portion of\nthe state highway system to Assembly Member Bobby D'Andrea\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill dedicates the bridge crossing interstate 87 on Union Avenue in\nSaratoga Springs to the late Assembly Member Bobby D'Andrea.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 dedicates the bridge on State Route 9P crossing Interstate 87\nin Saratoga Springs to the late Assembly Member Bobby D'Andrea.\n\nSection 2 provides for signage but specifies that the official name of\nthe bridge, BIN 1007069, will not be changed.\n\nSection 3 provides an effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nTechnical changes have been made to Section 1.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAssembly Member Bobby D'Andrea was a much beloved businessman, civic\nleader and Member of the Assembly for Saratoga Springs and surrounding\ncommunities. This bill would dedicate the bridge on the Union Avenue\ngateway into Saratoga Springs to Assembly Member D'Andrea, who passed\naway at the age of 92 in March 2025. He was an active participant in his\ncommunity as an entrepreneur who owned and operated the Kaydeross Amuse-\nment Park for 30 years, a county supervisor representing Saratoga\nSprings, the president of the Principessa Elena Society, the director of\nthe Saratoga Lake Association, the chair of the Fort Hudson Foundation,\nthe president of the United Community Fund and the president of the\nSaratoga County Task Force on Alzheimer's Disease. He represented the\ncity of Saratoga Springs, the Saratoga County towns of Wilton, Moreau,\nCorinth, Saratoga, and Northumberland, and all of Washington County in\nthe New York State Assembly for an incredible 14 terms, from 1974 to his\nretirement in 2001. A man of great compassion, optimism, and determi-\nnation, Assembly Member Bobby D'Andrea's legacy extends far beyond his\naccomplishments as a public servant. His compassion, his sincere concern\nfor others, his integrity and his motivation to give of his time and\nenergy stands as a beacon for those who aspire to serve their communi-\nties.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
